comments[3]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-19T22:21:25.931Z","harness:codex","Duplicate check: measured orientation plus complete207 open and0 active items and request-specific searches find no live declaration-state owner. Full closed pm-odw3j8 and recovery-parent metadata/history were read. This is a residual type contract newly identified by review comment4319454760 on PR1508, not a reopening or runtime-failure claim."
  "2026-10-19T22:23:10.191Z","harness:codex","Isolated pre-fix declaration control fails on all nine impossible status/field combinations: nine unused expected-error directives, plus three failed narrowing assignments. The same public root/core declaration test is retained. Replace the interface with exact/feasible_only/unavailable variants, require unavailable causes, and retain runtime safe-integer/equal-exact-budget validation. This changes declarations only; the private unavailable helper requires a non-null cause to match its existing callers."
  "2026-10-19T22:26:49.221Z","harness:codex",All four TypeScript projects and both linked commands pass; the runtime cohort retains189 cases with all existing numeric-guard and whitelist assertions. Public root/core tests now reject all nine inconsistent shapes and narrow status-dependent fields. A fresh npm tarball installed in an isolated consumer compiles those same declarations successfully. Strict ESLint contracts SDK-surface check and docs links pass. The snapshot explicitly acknowledges two declaration signatures for this newly introduced not-yet-published type. Comment-free JavaScript from all three touched runtime files is byte-identical to accepted native dd097e4e1; no runtime guard numeric policy or adapter whitelist changed.
